WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.910
Why isn't Obi-Wan Kenobi pulling out his lightsaber?

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:06.210
Where is this missing inquisitor?

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:09.210
And did anyone notice the new adorable droid?

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:13.970
These are the details they slipped by you
in the second Obi-Wan Kenobi trailer.

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:18.190
The new trailer marks the first glimpse of
comedy actor Kumail Nanjiani.

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:23.220
And if his wardrobe is anything to go by,
the Force might be with him too.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:26.240
Nanjiani can be seen hunkered down, seemingly
in hiding.

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:30.631
Interestingly, his character, who has yet
to be named, is wearing threads similar to

00:00:30.631 --> 00:00:32.660
the now eradicated Jedi.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:37.480
Might Nanjiani's character be one of the few,
like Obi-Wan Kenobi, that escaped the fallout

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.039
from Order 66?

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:44.059
If so, being the last remnant of the ancient
order is no laughing matter.

00:00:44.059 --> 00:00:48.850
This series could mark the actor taking on
a more serious and less quippy role than his

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:53.550
fans are used to — and it may spell doom
for his character's fate, given the risks

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:58.050
of being a Jedi in this scary post-"Revenge
of the Sith" world.

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:03.089
The highly anticipated reunion between Obi-Wan
and Darth Vader is not the only obstacle the

00:01:03.089 --> 00:01:05.410
Jedi Knight will have to face in the new series.

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:09.590
Fans of "Star Wars: Rebels" will recognize
the Inquisitors' return to the "Star Wars"

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:10.590
narrative.

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:15.410
Many Inquisitors had once been Jedi themselves,
but after Order 66, they joined the Empire,

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:21.370
and used their force sensitivity to hunt down
the remaining Jedi and other threats to the Empire.

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:28.670
"The Jedi knights are all but destroyed and
yet your task is not complete, Inquisitor."

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:33.061
Though Inquisitors are featured heavily in
the "Obi-Wan Kenobi" trailer, there is one

00:01:33.061 --> 00:01:35.140
character who is missing.

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:39.860
Seventh Sister was a main antagonist in the
animated series, but she is nowhere to be

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:41.350
seen in the new trailer.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:45.820
Considering the inclusion of both the High
Inquisitor and Fifth Brother who both appeared

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:48.700
in "Rebels," this omission may seem odd.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:52.600
Many fans on Reddit have commented on their
hope to see an appearance of the character.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:55.670
However, there is some logic to her absence.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:02:00.110
When Ezra first encounters her in "Rebels,"
Seventh Sister has a specific mission.

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:04.421
Many of the Inquisitors are trying to kidnap
force sensitive children but Seventh Sister

00:02:04.421 --> 00:02:07.960
is also on the hunt for Anakin's former padawan,
Ahsoka Tano.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:11.860
This could explain Seventh Sister's absence
in the events of "Obi-Wan Kenobi."

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:17.480
It might indicate that she'll instead be appearing
in the Ahsoka Tano Disney+ series.

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:22.409
While Kylo Ren's fiery lightsaber design in
the sequel trilogy is definitely one for the

00:02:22.409 --> 00:02:27.870
books, "Star Wars" die-hards know that there's
no characters who play with lightsaber construction

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:30.659
more creatively than the Inquisitors.

00:02:30.659 --> 00:02:35.719
The Grand Inquisitor's lightsaber has a circular
motor of some sort surrounding its handle,

00:02:35.719 --> 00:02:39.269
allowing the lightsaber to rotate like a helicopter's
blades.

00:02:39.269 --> 00:02:43.980
It seems that Inquisitor Reva's lightsaber
may serve a similar function — as shots

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:48.310
of her using her weapon in the trailer show
a similar half-circle handle guard of some

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:51.769
kind extending from one end of the lightsaber's
handle.

00:02:51.769 --> 00:02:56.020
Given the way actress Moses Ingram and the
series' executive producers have hyped up

00:02:56.020 --> 00:03:01.462
the character in recent months, expect it
to be used to help make Reva a uniquely terrifying villain.

00:03:01.462 --> 00:03:06.519
"Obi-Wan Kenobi" series writer and executive
producer Joby Harold recently told Entertainment

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:10.620
Weekly that Reva's addition to the franchise
will be a touchstone point in the history

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.170
of Star Wars bad guys.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:16.900
Ingram, for her part, described the character
as athletic and driven toward completing her

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:22.849
mission: it doesn't appear unreasonable to
think Reva may be the one to truly give Kenobi

00:03:22.849 --> 00:03:25.132
a tough time throughout the series.

00:03:25.132 --> 00:03:29.871
Another new "Star Wars" project, another cute
droid to merchandise, another toy to add to

00:03:29.871 --> 00:03:30.871
your collection.

00:03:30.871 --> 00:03:36.200
This brand-new droid has an interesting red-and-white
design with flaps on its back end that almost

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.090
appear to move like ears.

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:42.300
Between the red color scheme and black gloved
hand that it appears in, it seems safe to

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:47.030
assume this droid belongs to one of the Inquisitors,
if not Reva herself.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:52.709
Throughout nine "Star Wars" films, multiple
Disney+ live-action series, and any number

00:03:52.709 --> 00:03:58.029
of animated shows Lucasfilms has produced
over the years, we've seen droids do everything

00:03:58.029 --> 00:04:02.830
from repairing pod racers to piloting ships
to scouting out enemies — surely this one

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:07.129
will serve a unique purpose toward the galaxy-wide
search for Kenobi.

00:04:07.129 --> 00:04:11.260
If the new droid looks slightly familiar,
it may be due to the fact that it somewhat

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:15.540
resembles the very top of a BB unit without
the ball underneath that it rolls under — the

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:19.639
noises it makes certainly don't fall too far
from how BB-8 sounds throughout the three

00:04:19.639 --> 00:04:21.510
most recent "Star Wars" movies.

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:26.389
Those take place decades after the new "Obi-Wan
Kenobi" series, though: perhaps this droid

00:04:26.389 --> 00:04:30.560
design is a precursor to the lovable rolling
ball that accompanies Poe Dameron throughout

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:33.410
the galaxy in the sequel trilogy.

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:37.889
Between this trailer and the first hair-raising
teaser we got a few weeks back, one thing

00:04:37.889 --> 00:04:43.961
that both previews are missing is something
no Jedi should be without, and that's a lightsaber

00:04:43.961 --> 00:04:46.120
— Obi-Wan's, to be exact.

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:50.020
While Anakin Skywalker's former master looks
to be getting into plenty of trouble in the

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:55.229
new trailer, he's keeping most threats at
bay thanks to having a trusty blaster at his side.

00:04:55.229 --> 00:04:58.250
"So uncivilized."

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:00.930
This begs the question — what is going on?

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:05.120
Given that Kenobi is undoubtedly trying to
stay out of sight of the Empire, it's definitely

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:08.900
true that firing up his lightsaber might not
be the smartest move.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:12.000
Is there a chance that
there's more to it than that?

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:16.060
The last time we saw Kenobi sheath his weapon,
he'd left Anakin screaming in agony on the

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:20.903
shores of Mustafar, and watched the collapse
of everything he'd spent his life fighting for.

00:05:20.903 --> 00:05:25.780
Did the infamous duel have a lasting effect
on the old Jedi Knight, making him reluctant

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:27.199
to draw arms again?

00:05:27.199 --> 00:05:31.629
Could the teased reunion between master and
former apprentice cause old friends to draw

00:05:31.629 --> 00:05:33.000
swords once again?

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:36.629
It might just happen if our hero is forced
to do so.

